      "id": "claim_26fca722c4af48b4905424d39ad1de17",
      "statement": "If Spring Security is on the classpath, then web applications are secured by default. This includes securing Spring Boot’s /error endpoint. Spring Boot relies on Spring Security’s content-negotiation strategy to determine whether to use httpBasic or formLogin. To add method-level security to a web application, you can also add @EnableMethodSecurity with your desired settings. Additional information can be found in the Spring Security Reference Guide.",
